  <header class="top"><div class="shell top-inner"><a class="brand" href="index.php"><span>L</span>LChat</a><nav><a href="index.php">Open messenger</a><a href="#methods">Methods API</a></nav></div></header>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Developer documentation</div><h1>LChat Bot API</h1><p>Create a bot via <strong>@BotCreator</strong>, receive personal API-token and reply to messages from your PHP-script or other server.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="index.php">Find @BotCreator →</a><a class="button secondary" href="#quickstart">Quick start</a></div></section>
    <div class="layout"><aside class="toc"><b>Contents</b><a href="#quickstart">Quick start</a><a href="#creator">Commands BotCreator</a><a href="#auth">Token and requests</a><a href="#methods">Methods API</a><a href="#examples">Examples</a><a href="#limits">Restrictions</a></aside><main class="content">
      <section id="quickstart" class="section"><h2>Quick start</h2><ol class="steps"><li>Log in LChat and find the user <strong>@BotCreator</strong> via chat search. You can also open <strong>🤖 My bots → Write @BotCreator</strong>.</li><li>Send <code>/newbot</code>, then the name and free login, which ends with <code>bot</code>.</li><li>Copy the token from the response. To check, call <code>getMe</code>.</li><li>Open a personal chat with a new bot or add it to your group/channel through the menu <strong>My bots</strong>. After this, the bot will begin to receive messages via <code>getUpdates</code>.</li></ol><p class="note">The token gives full access to the bot’s actions. Keep it on the server, don’t paste it into HTML or browser JavaScript.</p></section>
      <section id="creator" class="section"><h2>@BotCreator</h2><p>This is a service account inside LChat. Commands are sent via regular messages in a personal chat with him; a separate password for the bot is not needed.</p><div class="commands"><code>/start</code><span>Show greeting and available commands.</span><code>/newbot</code><span>Create a bot: BotCreator will ask for your name and login, then display API-token.</span><code>/mybots</code><span>List of your bots.</span><code>/token @helperbot</code><span>Issue a new token. The old one will stop working immediately.</span><code>/setname @helperbot New name</code><span>Change your bot’s display name.</span><code>/cancel</code><span>Cancel bot creation.</span></div><p>One user can create up to 10 bots. The login begins with a Latin letter, contains Latin letters, numbers or underscores and ends with <code>bot</code>.</p></section>
      <section id="auth" class="section"><h2>Authorization and response format</h2><p>Base address: <code>https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=METHOD</code>. Pass the token with the header <code>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN</code>. Address is also supported <code>https://chat.lbs.su/bot&lt;TOKEN&gt;/&lt;METHOD&gt;</code>, if the rules <code>.htaccess</code> work on hosting.</p><p>The answer is always JSON: <code>{"ok":true,"result":...}</code> or <code>{"ok":false,"error_code":400,"description":"..."}</code>. Dispatch methods accept JSON or form fields.</p></section>
      <section id="methods" class="section"><h2>Methods API</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>HTTP</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>getMe</code>, <code>getChat</code></td><td>GET</td><td>Bot and available chat data.</td></tr><tr><td><code>getChats</code></td><td>GET</td><td><code>after, limit</code> — List of bot chats. For the next page, pass the last one ID c after.</td></tr><tr><td><code>getChatMemberCount</code></td><td>GET</td><td><code>chat_id</code> — Number of participants.</td></tr><tr><td><code>getChatMember</code></td><td>GET</td><td><code>chat_id, user_id</code> — Data and role of the participant.</td></tr><tr><td><code>getMessage</code></td><td>GET</td><td><code>chat_id, message_id</code> — Read the message after the bot joins.</td></tr><tr><td><code>setMessageReaction</code></td><td>POST</td><td><code>chat_id, message_id, emoji</code> — Put 👍 ❤️ 😂 😮 😢 or 👏. Meaning null removes reaction.</td></tr><tr><td><code>editMessageCaption</code></td><td>POST</td><td><code>chat_id, message_id, caption</code> — Change the bot media signature. Up to 1024 characters. An empty line clears the signature.</td></tr><tr><td><code>getUpdates</code></td><td>GET</td><td>Queue of messages and button presses; <code>offset</code>, <code>limit</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>setWebhook</code>, <code>deleteWebhook</code>, <code>getWebhookInfo</code></td><td>POST / GET</td><td>HTTPS-webhook, disconnection and delivery status.</td></tr><tr><td><code>sendMessage</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Text, inline-buttons or regular keyboard under the input field.</td></tr><tr><td><code>sendDocument</code>, <code>sendPhoto</code>, <code>sendAudio</code>, <code>sendVideo</code>, <code>sendVoice</code>, <code>sendAnimation</code></td><td>POST</td><td>File via multipart or available <code>file_id</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>getFile</code></td><td>GET</td><td>File metadata and download path.</td></tr><tr><td><code>editMessageText</code>, <code>editMessageReplyMarkup</code>, <code>deleteMessage</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Change text or buttons, delete your own message.</td></tr><tr><td><code>answerCallbackQuery</code></td><td>POST</td><td>Reply to the user after clicking inline-buttons.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>For <code>getUpdates</code> use <code>offset</code>, equal to the last one <code>update_id + 1</code>, and <code>limit</code> from 1 to 100. Save offset on the side of your bot. Poll is disabled when webhook is active.</p></section>
      <section id="examples" class="section"><h2>Examples of requests</h2><h3>Token verification</h3><pre>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" "https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=getMe"</pre><h3>Receiving messages</h3><pre>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" "https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=getUpdates&amp;offset=0"</pre><h3>Sending a reply</h3><pre>curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"chat_id":123,"text":"Hello!"}' "https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=sendMessage"</pre><p><code>chat_id</code> can be taken from the field <code>message.chat.id</code> answer <code>getUpdates</code>. Start the survey with a pause between requests.</p></section>
      <section class="section"><h2>Examples of new functions</h2><p>Webhook: send using <code>setWebhook</code> JSON <code>{"url":"https://example.com/hook","secret_token":"my-secret"}</code>. Accept POST with object <code>message</code> or <code>callback_query</code>; check the title <code>X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token</code> and answer HTTP 2xx.</p><pre>curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" -F "chat_id=123" -F "document=@photo.png" "https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=sendDocument"</pre><p>Inline-buttons are transferred to the field <code>reply_markup</code>:</p><pre>{"inline_keyboard":[[{"text":"Done","callback_data":"done"},{"text":"Website","url":"https://example.com"}]]}</pre><p>Respond to pressing using the method <code>answerCallbackQuery</code>, passing <code>callback_query_id</code> and <code>text</code>.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>Regular bot keyboard</h2><p>Transfer to <code>sendMessage.reply_markup</code> object <code>{"keyboard":[[{"text":"Help"},{"text":"Profile"}]],"resize_keyboard":true}</code>. Buttons will appear above the input field; clicking will send the text of the selected button to the bot. For a one-time keyboard, specify <code>one_time_keyboard:true</code>, and for a hint — <code>input_field_placeholder</code>. You can remove buttons by sending a message to <code>{"remove_keyboard":true}</code>.</p></section><section id="limits" class="section"><h2>Delivery and compatibility</h2><p>The bot sees new messages only in chats where it was added. You can choose a short survey <code>getUpdates</code> or <code>setWebhook</code> with public HTTPS-address. Webhook sends JSON via cURL upon request; for repetitions in the absence of new requests, run <code>php tools/bot-webhook-worker.php</code> by cron. Secret title <code>X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token</code> supported.</p><p>Files - up to 8 MB, total bot limit - 200 MB. Inline-buttons support HTTPS-link and <code>callback_data</code>. The methods listed above are implemented, but fully compatible with all methods Telegram Bot API, including payments and stickers, not yet available. After moving to a new queue, old messages are not reissued.</p></section>
      <section id="temporary-sites" class="section"><h2>Temporary sites for 10 minutes</h2><p>A bot can publish an isolated project using the <code>createTemporarySite</code>. Pass on <code>owner_user_id</code>, name and object <code>files</code>. The answer contains HTTPS-link of the form <code>/apis/bots/pages/temps/sites/30_CHARACTERS/</code> and time of removal. Available HTML, CSS, JS, JSON, TXT, SVG and safe PHP-templates. free PHP-functions, network, database and file system are not available.</p><pre>curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"owner_user_id":123,"name":"Demo","files":{"index.html":"&lt;h1&gt;Hello&lt;/h1&gt;"}}' "https://chat.lbs.su/bot-api.php?method=createTemporarySite"</pre><p>List: <code>getTemporarySites?owner_user_id=123</code>. Early removal: <code>deleteTemporarySite</code> with fields <code>owner_user_id</code> and <code>site_id</code>. Limitation of one project: 20 files and 1 MiB; the number of consecutive publications is not limited.</p></section>
    </main></div>
